&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PandaDoc&#39;s Brand Studio is looking for a versatile designer to be our Brand Designer, Production.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast. Our Brand Studio supports campaigns, paid media, events, web, and more — often all at once — and we need a designer who can keep up without losing quality. This role is the engine that keeps creative output moving: you&#39;ll own production across a wide range of assets and formats, context-switch between projects without missing a beat, and occasionally bring your own creative thinking to the table when the brief calls for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a pure production role. We need someone well-rounded enough to fill gaps across the team — whether that&#39;s finishing a paid ad set, creating marketing collateral, or jumping into a campaign with a fresh idea. You&#39;re flexible, fast, and care about craft even on the smallest asset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report into the Design Lead on the Brand Studio team, which sits within Corporate Marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner closely with the paid media team: &lt;/strong&gt;Work hand-in-hand with paid media to understand what&#39;s performing, adapt quickly, and apply those learnings to make the next round of assets sharper. You pay attention to what works and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own day-to-day production output:&lt;/strong&gt; Execute a high volume of brand and marketing assets across formats — paid ads, social graphics, email headers, event signage, presentation decks, sales collateral, and more. You&#39;re reliable, consistent, and fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context-switch without dropping the ball:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll regularly move between multiple projects and priorities. You know how to triage, stay organized, and deliver on time without needing someone to manage every detail for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay current on tools, AI, and production best practices: &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re always looking for smarter ways to work — whether that&#39;s a new AI design tool, a faster way to batch assets, or a process that cuts review cycles. You bring that knowledge back to the team and help raise the bar on how we produce at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support campaign and event creative:&lt;/strong&gt; Jump in on integrated campaigns and event activations to support the broader Brand Studio team — resizing, adapting, and producing assets that carry the creative vision through to final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring ideas when the brief calls for it:&lt;/strong&gt; This isn&#39;t a heads-down production seat. When there&#39;s room to concept or contribute a creative direction, you take it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain brand consistency:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply brand guidelines accurately and consistently across every asset you touch. You&#39;re a steward of the details — spacing, hierarchy, color, and type — even under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with brand designers, copywriters, and marketing stakeholders to get assets across the finish line. You communicate clearly, flag issues early, and make the team around you faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You embody our &lt;strong&gt;EPIC&lt;/strong&gt; values: you push for &lt;strong&gt;Excellence&lt;/strong&gt; even on the smallest deliverable, find &lt;strong&gt;Purpose&lt;/strong&gt; in keeping the creative engine running, embrace &lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt; by finding smarter ways to produce great work, and build &lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt; by being the teammate everyone wants on a deadline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll report into the Manager, Brand Design on the Brand Studio team, which sits within Corporate Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a student of the craft and the process. You keep up with AI design tools, production workflows, and emerging techniques — not out of FOMO, but because you genuinely want to find better ways to do the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fast without being sloppy. You know the difference between good enough and actually good — and you default to the latter even when time is tight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a context-switcher by nature. Jumping between a paid ad, an event banner, and a deck in the same afternoon doesn&#39;t stress you out. It&#39;s just Tuesday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re organized and self-directed. You don&#39;t need someone managing your queue for you. You know what&#39;s priority, what&#39;s in progress, and what&#39;s blocked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Details matter to you. Spacing, hierarchy, color, type — you bring visual judgment to every asset, not just the marquee projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of brand or graphic design experience, with a portfolio that demonstrates range across formats and channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Figma, Adobe Illustrator, and Photoshop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing assets across digital and print formats — paid ads, HTML5 banners, social, email, event materials, presentations, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work within and apply an established brand system accurately and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and comfort managing multiple concurrent projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in-house at a B2B SaaS or tech company preferred (agency experience considered)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus:&lt;/em&gt; Experience with motion design or basic animation in &lt;strong&gt;After Effects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus:&lt;/em&gt; Familiarity with AI design tools that accelerate production output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why PandaDoc?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PandaDoc, we&#39;re building the agreement platform for growing businesses — and we&#39;re investing in the brand to match that ambition. Through PandaDoc, we offer employees competitive compensation, best-in-class perks and benefits. We hire collaborative, customer-obsessed problem solvers and give you ample opportunity to grow and succeed. If you&#39;re passionate about craft, energized by brand building, and excited to make a difference, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PandaDoc empowers more than 60,000 growing organizations to thrive by taking the work out of document workflow. PandaDoc provides an all-in-one document workflow automation platform that helps fast scaling teams accelerate the ability to create, manage, and sign digital documents including proposals, quotes, contracts, and more.&amp;nbsp; For more information, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pandadoc.com&quot;&gt;https://www.pandadoc.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re known for our work-life balance, kind co-workers, &amp;amp; creative virtual team-bonding events. And although our Pandas are located across the globe, we stay connected with the help of technology and ensure that everyone on our team feels, well, like a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pandas work best when they&#39;re happy. We retain our talent by upholding our values of integrity &amp;amp; transparency, and selling a product that changes the lives of our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/pandadoc/life/pdcompanyculture&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees may be able to purchase company stock (or receive annual bonuses)&lt;br&gt;Employees (and their families) may enroll in the company&#39;s medical, dental, vision, short &amp;amp; long term disability, life insurance, FSA and 401k plans. Employees will also receive 13.34+ hours of paid time off per month, 6 self care days, birthday PTO day, and 12 company paid holidays off per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual range for this role is $95,000-$120,000 OTE, which includes both base and variable pay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PandaDoc is an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to equal treatment of all employees without regard to race, national origin, religion, gender, age, sexual orientation, veteran status, physical or mental disability or other basis protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deadline: 6/29/2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PandaDoc&#39;s Brand Studio is looking for a Brand Design Lead to join our team of creatives.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re evolving how PandaDoc shows up in the world — bolder, more cinematic, more human — and this role is central to making that real. You&#39;ll own the visual execution of our brand across key brand moments: out-of-home, events, integrated campaigns, and the big creative swings that define how the market sees us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior IC role. You&#39;ll concept, design, and art direct across a broad range of channels and mediums — bringing sharp creative thinking to brand campaigns while staying hands-on with execution. You&#39;re the kind of designer who can set the visual direction for a campaign and then see it through to final delivery. You&#39;re also fluent in AI-powered design tools and excited about building processes that increase creative velocity, volume, and quality without sacrificing craft. You&#39;ve designed across a broad spectrum of channels, mediums, and placements — OOH, digital, events, paid social, and beyond — and you know how to flex your thinking for each one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work as a peer to other Brand Studio leads, collaborating closely on visual identity, campaign creative, and cross-functional projects — reporting directly to the Creative Director on the Brand Studio team, which sits within Corporate Marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead brand campaigns:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the visual direction for our brand campaigns — integrated campaigns, out-of-home, events, experiential activations, and beyond — from brief through final delivery. You concept, design, and set the visual creative across a broad range of channels and mediums. You understand how a brand idea lives on a billboard, a trade show floor, and a paid social feed — and what each one needs to land.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborates across disciples:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with copywriters, video and motion creatives, and marketing stakeholders to bring integrated ideas to life. You give direction as clearly as you take it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to visual identity:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Brand Studio leadership on the evolution of PandaDoc&#39;s visual identity — typography, color, composition, photography direction, and design system guardrails. You&#39;re a steward of the brand, not just an executor of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain quality and consistency:&lt;/strong&gt; Review brand creative across the team and ensure everything going out the door reflects the standard we&#39;re building toward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build AI-powered design processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and implement AI tools that increase design output and creative velocity — from automating repetitive production tasks to exploring generative tools that accelerate concepting and iteration. You&#39;re not replacing craft with AI; you&#39;re using it to protect time for the work that actually requires it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You embody our &lt;strong&gt;EPIC&lt;/strong&gt; values: you push for &lt;strong&gt;Excellence&lt;/strong&gt; in craft and concept, find &lt;strong&gt;Purpose&lt;/strong&gt; in building a brand people recognize and trust, embrace &lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt; by bringing unexpected creative thinking to every brief, and build &lt;strong&gt;Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt; across Brand Studio, Marketing, and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll report into the Creative Director on the Brand Studio team, which sits within Corporate Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead with ideas. High caliber design matters, but concepting is where you start. Your portfolio shows original thinking across channels, not just polished production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fluent in campaign creative. You know how an idea lives across OOH, digital, social, and events — and you know where each medium needs something different.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity. Brand is evolving here, and you&#39;re energized by that — not waiting for a complete style guide before you do good work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about the details without losing the big picture. Kerning matters. So does whether the concept actually lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You give and receive creative feedback well — and you don&#39;t stop there. You use performance data, campaign learnings, and post-mortems to understand what&#39;s working and bring that thinking back into the next brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of brand or visual design experience, with a portfolio demonstrating strong campaign concepting and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing across a broad range of channels and placements — print media, OOH, digital, events, paid social, brand campaigns, and more. You&#39;re not a specialist in one format; you&#39;re fluent across all of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual sensibility — you can direct photography, establish tone, and give feedback that makes work sharper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in &lt;strong&gt;Figma&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Adobe Illustrator&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Photoshop&lt;/strong&gt;, and the broader Adobe Creative Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with design systems and brand governance — you&#39;ve helped evolve a visual identity, not just execute within one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in AI design tools and the ability to apply them to real production workflows — accelerating output without compromising craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in digital user experiences — landing pages, web, email&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in-house at a B2B SaaS or tech company (agency experience considered with strong brand portfolio)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus:&lt;/em&gt; Illustration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
